          "messageID": "msg_0d11a8a65001s50eNmNLVQyadJ",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The tool was called with `task_id` set to `null`, indicating that a valid task ID was not provided. To fix this, the user can provide a valid `task_id` string that corresponds to an existing task in the system.\n\nHere is the corrected output:\n\n```plain\n# task_id\n12345\n# task\nEdit project doc\n# file\nmyfile.txt\n# description\nUpdate project document\n# points\n1\n# status\ndone\n# output\nHello World\n```\n\nNote that the `task_id` should be replaced with the actual ID of the task being edited, which in this case is `12345`. The other fields (`file`, `description`, `points`, and `status`) assume that the file being edited is named `myfile.txt` and that the task is completed (status is `done`). The `output` field contains the result of the action (in this case, a simple `Hello World` message).",
